2026-09-24T01:52:34.8499590Z 
2026-09-24T01:52:34.8499697Z Start here:
2026-09-24T01:52:34.8500002Z   dw setup                           Connect DiffWitness to Claude/Codex/Cursor for this Git project
2026-09-24T01:52:34.8500409Z   dw status                          See what is known, unknown, and what to do next
2026-09-24T01:52:34.8500803Z After setup, use your coding agent normally; run `dw status` after a change.
2026-09-24T01:52:34.8501034Z 
2026-09-24T01:52:34.8501116Z Useful when needed:
2026-09-24T01:52:34.8501421Z   dw explain                         Explain the latest change from local evidence, with no AI required
2026-09-24T01:52:34.8501870Z   dw state why ID                     Find the recorded reasons and sources behind a memory item
2026-09-24T01:52:34.8502270Z   dw ask "question"                  Read cited project facts or an explicit abstention
2026-09-24T01:52:34.8502689Z   dw protect detect                  Check optional live protection without changing configuration
2026-09-24T01:52:34.8503123Z   dw view technical                  Open the complete engineering command surface
2026-09-24T01:52:34.8503352Z 
2026-09-24T01:52:34.8503535Z A blocked or observed runtime action is not proof that the final software works.
2026-09-24T01:52:34.8504066Z DiffWitness verifies the resulting Git change independently. Source code and raw prompts/diffs stay local by default.
2026-09-24T01:52:34.8504424Z 
2026-09-24T01:52:34.8504606Z For every command and advanced workflow: `dw view technical`, then `dw --help`.
2026-09-24T01:52:34.8504855Z 
2026-09-24T01:52:34.8505219Z Language: English by default. Save with `dw language en|fr`; override once with `dw --language en|fr <command>`. OS locale never selects product language.
